# The repository stores text with LF. This matters here rather than being a
# preference: the runtime image is assembled from POSIX shell scripts and the
# `gradlew` launcher, and a CRLF in either breaks at execution time — the shell
# reports `\r: command not found`, and Gradle's own wrapper refuses to start.
#
# `eol=lf` on the checkout side too, so a clone on Windows does not rewrite them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception: cmd.exe wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Anything that is not text must never be line-ending converted. Listed
# explicitly because `text=auto` guesses from content, and it guesses wrong on
# small binaries often enough to corrupt them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
*.aar binary
*.so binary
*.apk binary
*.deb binary
*.ttf binary
